OL,3,GNEWSAEscape of Charles II to be
OL,4,Arecreated by riders
OL,5,
OL,6,FA group of re-enactors on horseback
OL,7,Fplan to recreate one of the most famous
OL,8,Fmoments of the English Civil War.
OL,10,FIn September 1651 the man who later
OL,11,Fbecame King Charles II was forced to
OL,12,Fflee after defeat at the Battle of
OL,13,FWorcester, hiding in the branches of a
OL,14,Ftree along the way.
OL,16,FOn Sunday, members of the
OL,17,FWorcestershire Cavalry group, along
OL,18,Fwith descendants of members of the
OL,19,Foriginal royal party, will retrace part
OL,20,Fof that route.
OL,23,APub: 30-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
